[[Wyrm]]s are [[Draconic (attribute)|draconic]] creatures requiring 62 [[Slayer]] to harm. Players can choose to kill any of three different variants for a wyrms task: [[Wyrm]]s (sometimes referred to as adult wyrms), [[wyrmling]]s, and [[Lava Strykewyrm]]s.

==Monster variants==
'''Adult wyrms''' have a [[flat armour]] value of 1 and use both melee and magic attacks, using magic only when attacking from a distance. They have a [[Superior slayer monster|superior variant]], the [[Shadow Wyrm]], which cannot be safespotted and has 2 flat armour, but otherwise shares the same attacks and mechanics. Adult wyrms notably drop [[dragon shortsword]]s, [[Dragon harpoon|dragon harpoons]], [[Dragon knife|dragon knives]], and [[Dragon thrownaxe|dragon thrownaxes]].

'''Wyrmlings''' attack only with melee and do not have flat armour. Unlike adult wyrms, they do not have a superior variant and have no drops aside from their [[Wyrmling bones|bones]].

'''Lava Strykewyrms''' are aggressive, use ranged and melee attacks, and do not have flat armour. Their superior variant, the [[magma strykewyrm]], has a unique burrowing mechanic that requires the player to move at least two tiles from their position when the attack was initiated or they will take moderate damage. They drop [[dragon metal sheet]]s, with an increased drop rate while on a wyrms task.
